From: Paper Linux Maintainers <paper-linux@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: mc13892: preserve overlapping switcher range

The SW2-SW4 HI bit selects the voltage range shared by the normal, DVS and
standby selectors in each switcher register.  The current driver chooses the
low range for every request at or below 1.375 V, even when the requested
voltage is also representable in the already-selected high range.  This
unnecessarily changes how the two selectors not owned by the regulator are
interpreted.

Read the current switcher register under the existing lock and retain its high
range for voltages in the 1.1-1.375 V overlap.  A range change is still made
when the requested voltage cannot be represented by the current range.

This is required for the Kindle 3 CPU rail: its inherited SW2 normal, DVS and
standby slots are 1.35 V in the high range, and that voltage is valid in either
range.  Retaining the high range lets frequency scaling leave the two dormant
slots unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Paper Linux Maintainers <paper-linux@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/regulator/mc13892-regulator.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/regulator/mc13892-regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/mc13892-regulator.c
@@ -445,7 +445,7 @@
 {
 	struct mc13xxx_regulator_priv *priv = rdev_get_drvdata(rdev);
 	int volt, mask, id = rdev_get_id(rdev);
-	u32 reg_value;
+	u32 reg_value, val;
 	int ret;
 
 	volt = rdev->desc->volt_table[selector];
@@ -466,10 +466,28 @@
 	 * thing more readable and we do far less work.
 	 */
 
+	mc13xxx_lock(priv->mc13xxx);
+
 	if (mc13892_regulators[id].vsel_reg != MC13892_SWITCHERS0) {
 		mask |= MC13892_SWITCHERS0_SWxHI;
 
-		if (volt > 1375000) {
+		ret = mc13xxx_reg_read(priv->mc13xxx,
+					 mc13892_regulators[id].vsel_reg, &val);
+		if (ret)
+			goto out;
+
+		/*
+		 * The HI bit selects the voltage range for all three voltage
+		 * slots in a switcher register.  Preserve the current range when
+		 * the requested voltage is representable in both ranges, avoiding
+		 * an otherwise unnecessary reinterpretation of the DVS and standby
+		 * selectors.
+		 */
+		if (volt >= 1100000 && volt <= 1375000 &&
+		    (val & MC13892_SWITCHERS0_SWxHI)) {
+			reg_value -= MC13892_SWxHI_SEL_OFFSET;
+			reg_value |= MC13892_SWITCHERS0_SWxHI;
+		} else if (volt > 1375000) {
 			reg_value -= MC13892_SWxHI_SEL_OFFSET;
 			reg_value |= MC13892_SWITCHERS0_SWxHI;
 		} else {
@@ -477,9 +495,10 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	mc13xxx_lock(priv->mc13xxx);
 	ret = mc13xxx_reg_rmw(priv->mc13xxx, mc13892_regulators[id].vsel_reg,
 			      mask, reg_value);
+
+out:
 	mc13xxx_unlock(priv->mc13xxx);
 
 	return ret;
-- 
